equeños. Su figura de transición fue Davy Graham, cuya «Angi» (1962) se volvió el estándar de los guitarristas acústicos y que introdujo la afinación DADGAD para imitar el oud que oyó en Marruecos. Les Cousins, abierto en Greek Street el 16 de abril de 1965 como club de toda la noche, fue refugio de fugados y adolescentes de suburbio y semillero de Bert Jansch, Paul Simon, Jackson C. Frank, Roy Harper, Donovan, Sandy Denny, Mick Softley y Anne Briggs: romanticismo maldito, sin temas tabú (prostitución masculina, heroína, salud mental). La trabajadora social Judith Piepe acogía en su piso de Cable Street a Simon, Al Stewart, Denny y Frank.","color":"#a3e635","family":"Folk rock y canción protesta","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/1966/#les-cousins"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":253743264980767,"artist":"Al Stewart","artist_id":189567235419416,"title":"Pretty Golden Hair","year":1965,"ess":0,"yt":"5KIQinbP8B4","kind":null,"book":{"id":1,"title":"1966: The Year the Decade Exploded","author":"Jon Savage","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/1966/"},"scene":"Les Cousins y el nuevo folk británico","scene_id":247878389331910,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/1966/#les-cousins","chapters":["Enero: A Quiet Explosion: la CND, la protesta y la conspiración del silencio"],"pages":[[1,27],[1,402],[1,502]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"1966: The Year the Decade Exploded","author":"Jon Savage","page":27,"text":"…yet soon to trip into inner space. No subject was taboo in the repertoire of the Les Cousins regulars: there were songs about male prostitution (Al Stewart’s ‘Pretty Golden Hair’), drug addiction (Bert Jansch’s ‘Needle of Death’), isolation (Paul Simon’s ‘I Am a Rock’), mental-health policy (Roy…"},{"book":"1966: The Year the Decade Exploded","author":"Jon Savage","page":27,"text":"…of the Les Cousins crowd: her flat in Cable Street was open house for anyone who wanted to crash. Among those who stayed there were Sandy Denny, Al Stewart and the transplanted Americans Paul Simon and Jackson C. Frank. The interconnections would result in a couple of extraordinary 1965 albums: The Paul Simon Songbook and Jackson C. Frank, which was produced by Simon with Al Stewart on second guitar. It is Piepe’s voice who introduces the BBC clip of Stewart performing ‘Pretty Golden Hair’: ‘These troubadours of the 1960s sing to win your love for the unloved, the despised, the rejected. The outsider…"},{"book":"1966: The Year the Decade Exploded","author":"Jon Savage","page":402,"text":"…to Tom Salmon about her work among young people in the clubs of Soho and was shown at 6.15 p.m. on 20 November 1966 Judith Piepe’s voiceover and Al Stewart singing ‘Pretty Golden Hair’ can be seen at www.youtube.com/watch?v=b4zULQipyM8 The Top of the Pops video that showed Dylan arriving at London…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":114608586539496,"type":"album","name":"Bed Sitter Images","list_id":35507544569942,"list":"RYM Top — Pop — Baroque Pop","src":"musthear","rank":175,"year":1967,"note":null,"yt":"mBEK2hOUVOM","scaruffi":null},{"id":114608586539496,"type":"album","name":"Bed Sitter Images","list_id":233564640149435,"list":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements — Second British Folk Revival","src":"musthear","rank":195,"year":1967,"note":null,"yt":"mBEK2hOUVOM","scaruffi":null},{"id":173190439550824,"type":"album","name":"Love Chronicles","list_id":136210250045982,"list":"RYM Top — Pop — Folk Pop","src":"musthear","rank":123,"year":1969,"note":null,"yt":"gxMfnLmo1f4","scaruffi":null},{"id":173190439550824,"type":"album","name":"Love Chronicles","list_id":233564640149435,"list":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements — Second British Folk Revival","src":"musthear","rank":132,"year":1969,"note":null,"yt":"gxMfnLmo1f4","scaruffi":null},{"id":169077814897197,"type":"album","name":"Zero She Flies","list_id":136210250045982,"list":"RYM Top — Pop — Folk Pop","src":"musthear","rank":165,"year":1970,"note":null,"yt":"M-2BGTw53gY","scaruffi":null},{"id":169077814